   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the estates, powers and trusts law, in relation to creating an\nalternative method to compromising an award issued by the September 11th\nVictim Compensation Fund (\"VCF\")",
    "basePrintNo": "S6810",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6810-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §5-4.6, EPT L",
    "lawSection": "Estates, Powers and Trusts Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6810\n\nSPONSOR: GOUNARDES\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the estates, powers and trusts law, in relation to\ncreating an alternative method to compromising an award issued by the\nSeptember 11th Victim Compensation Fund (\"VCF\")\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe proposed legislation would create an alternative simplified method\nfor the family of victims to settle and collect a VCF award that\nconsists entirely of non-economic losses.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 5-4.6 of the Estates, Powers, and Trusts Law\nwhich relates to the application to compromise an action.\n\nSection two sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, under New York's wrongful death statute, an award issued by\nthe VCF is treated the same as any action for wrongful act, neglect or\ndefault causing the death of a decedent. Once an award is issued by the\nVCF, the personal representative must apply to the Surrogate's Court for\na court order allowing the compromise, collection, and distribution of\nthe award. The Surrogate's Court is responsible to ensure the adequacy\nof the award and the proper allocation of the funds to the interested\nparties.\n\nThis bill seeks to create a simplified alternative method for VCF awards\nthat consists solely of non-economic losses (i.e. emotional damages) to\nbe distributed to the family of 9/11 victims without unnecessary delay.\nIt also seeks to minimize the administrative burden on the family, VCF,\nand the Surrogate's Court. The VCF issues a very detailed award break-\ndown and allocation of the award between economic loss and non-economic\nloss. Non-economic losses are due to the estate of the decedent and\ndistributed pursuant to the decedent's will or the laws of intestacy, if\nthe decedent died without a will. Therefore where the award consists\nentirely of non-economic losses, the personal representative should be\nallowed to collect the award without a lengthy compromise proceeding. A\nsimplified method in lieu of a compromise proceeding can address the\nissue of the adequacy of the award and protection of any distributee who\nmay be under a disability without the burdensome compromise process.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nIf enacted, this proposed legislation would create administrative\nsavings in the VCF and the Surrogate's Court due to a simplified step in\nthe VCF claims process.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate\n",
